# Services

## File layout

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `index.go` | Interface + private struct + constructor |
| `service.go` | Implementation (`service_{feature}.go` if large) |
| `payload.go` | Request DTOs with `validate` tags |
| `response.go` | Response DTOs |
| `transformer.go` | Model → response (optional) |

## Constructor pattern (matches role/index.go)

```go
type roleService struct {
    txRepo                tx.TxRepo
    roleRepo              role.RoleRepo
    accountService        account.AccountService
    rolePermissionService role_permission.RolePermissionService
}

func NewRoleService(
    txRepo tx.TxRepo,
    roleRepo role.RoleRepo,
    accountService account.AccountService,
    rolePermissionService role_permission.RolePermissionService,
) RoleService { ... }
```

## Return types

- Prefer `*Response` or `*transformer.Pagination` for handler-facing methods.
- `*model.X` is acceptable for simple internal CRUD when no response DTO exists yet.
- Never return GORM types to handlers from repos directly — always through service.

## Transactions

```go
return s.txRepo.Run(ctx, func(ctx context.Context) error {
    if err := s.userRepo.Create(ctx, m); err != nil { return err }
    return nil
})
```

## Cross-domain + error checks

```go
accountData, err := s.accountService.GetAccountByID(ctx, roleData.AccountID)
if err != nil && !errors.Is(err, "DATA_NOT_FOUND") {
    return nil, err
}
```

## Rules

- `context.Context` first on every method
- No Fiber imports
- DRY; skip pointless helpers
- Register new codes in `registry.go`
